+### Optimizer slots
+
+Optimization has three slots. Each one is a name you can swap without changing anything else:
+
+| Slot | Acts on | Choices today |
+|------|---------|---------------|
+| `input` | command output, files and logs before they enter context | `none`, `proxy`, `headroom`, `rtk` |
+| `context` | the accumulated conversation | `none` |
+| `output` | what the model writes | `none` |
+
+`none` is always valid and is the baseline every comparison uses. `proxy` is whatever you configured in `[compression.plugin]`; `headroom` is the built-in default plugin. Pick one per slot in `.ta/daemon.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[optimizers.input]
+use = "none"        # none | proxy | headroom | rtk
+```
+
+With no `[optimizers.input]`, the input slot follows `[compression]`: `proxy` if `[compression.plugin]` is set, `headroom` if compression is enabled, otherwise `none`. An unknown name is refused with the list of valid ones. Only `proxy` and `headroom` start a supervised process. `rtk` is selectable and its licence is recorded, but TA does not launch or install it: agent API calls go direct while it is selected.
+
+Licences recorded for the starters (confirm against each project before redistributing): headroom Apache-2.0, RTK (`rtk-oss`) Apache-2.0. The full `rtk` and `rtk-proxy` builds add BUSL-1.1 components, so check which one you install.
+
+Compare a slot choice with a golden replay, without touching your config:
+
+```bash
+ta golden replay <id> --set optimizers.input.use=none
+ta golden replay <id> --set optimizers.input.use=headroom
+ta golden report <id>
+```
+
+The override is checked before anything is launched and applies only to that replay's goal.
+
+Every optimizer application produces a metrics record (`bytes_in`, `bytes_out`, `est_tokens_in`, `est_tokens_out`, `ms`, `lossless`, `original_ref`). The full original is kept on disk under `original_ref`, so any reduction can be reversed or audited. Token figures are estimates (about 4 bytes per token) for comparing optimizers, not billing numbers. The traits and registry live in the `ta-context-opt` crate.
+
 ### Windows installer
 
 The Windows `.msi` installer includes an optional "Enable context compression (headroom)" checkbox that runs `pip install headroom-ai[all]` during setup. The checkbox is checked by default.
